0304001-cc09c36a-9282-4278-b2df-7e1db8cb7ea3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"8252d1181b2798968ea6bd9b8e7d9ecafe06a99e7d16bc1c53c7be969a38a78c","event_uuid":"ec6812ad-d761-48b2-96fa-4131581e7b03","position":{"commit_sha":"946a187888841ebdab92f7c7afacd729e115885f","position":"1787600379124216001-ec6812ad-d761-48b2-96fa-4131581e7b03"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787594504225041001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"bfdf89c0-2a3b-4c21-b943-c8d694322b0a","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"},{"link_uuid":"cc09c36a-9282-4278-b2df-7e1db8cb7ea3","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"b173-e50a-4b93-455f"}],"description":"Update AGENTS.md + docs (epic items 6–7) once the ADR (deft-evolutive-mosasaur) and trusted-env\nregistration land: require using the MCP server for all rebar operations EXCEPT operations that need\nlocal code (testing, investigation, debugging, validation), and state the certified-op policy\ncorrectly. Single concern: guidance + user-facing docs — no server/infra behavior here.\n\n## Scope + rationale\n1. **AGENTS.md MCP-required policy**: a rule that rebar tracker operations go through the MCP server,\n   with the explicit carve-out for local-code ops (test/investigate/debug/validate). Because this\n   introduces a new prohibition (\"don't drive the tracker by ad-hoc local CLI when MCP is\n   available\"), do the new-prohibition **consumer scan**: enumerate the existing guidance/workflows\n   that tell agents to run `rebar ...` locally and reconcile each (update or carve out), so the rule\n   doesn't contradict standing instructions.\n2. **Certified-op wording correction**: certified **plan-review** and **completion-verifier** ops\n   (the only two op-cert kinds, ADR 0049) route through the MCP server and are enforceable because\n   the box is a registered trusted signing environment (the trusted-env slice). **Code review is the\n   Gerrit `LLM-Review` vote, NOT an op-cert** — correct the epic's item-7 phrasing (\"code review ...\n   certified through the MCP server\") so guidance doesn't imply a nonexistent code-review op-cert.\n3. **docs/mcp-auth.md**: fill the §7 \"AWS-specific deployment\" gap with the ADR-decided recipe\n   (nginx `/mcp/` TLS edge + `static` verifier + per-client bearer). Add a NEW client-connection\n   guide (copilot/codex/claude config shapes from olm), which docs/mcp-auth.md currently lacks.\n\n## Prior-art / doc-drift check (blocking prior-art overlay)\nGit history shows the hand-authored MCP docs carry modest recurring upkeep; keep the AWS recipe and\nclient guide close to the single-sourced config keys the ADR names so they don't drift. Match the\nexisting docs/mcp-auth.md structure rather than inventing a parallel doc.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] AGENTS.md states the MCP-required rule + the local-code carve-out; the consumer scan is recorded\n  (each pre-existing \"run rebar locally\" instruction is either updated or explicitly carved out —\n  oracle: a grep of the guidance shows no surviving instruction that contradicts the new rule).\n- [ ] The certified-op section names plan-review + completion-verifier as MCP-routed/enforceable-via\n  trusted-env and code-review as the Gerrit vote (NOT an op-cert), with no reference to a\n  code-review op-cert anywhere in guidance (oracle: grep for \"code review\" op-cert phrasing returns\n  none).\n- [ ] docs/mcp-auth.md §7 contains the AWS deploy recipe with the ADR-named config keys, and a\n  client-connection guide documents the three client config shapes.\n\n## Compat / rollback\nDocs-only; rollback = revert the doc edits. No behavior change.\n\nDepends on: deft-evolutive-mosasaur (ADR decides routing/auth), and the trusted-env registration\nslice (guidance claims certified ops are enforceable via MCP, which is only true once the box is a\ntrusted env).","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["depends_on","a45f-bd45-513a-49cb"],["depends_on","b173-e50a-4b93-455f"],["parent","jira-reb-3527"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"jira-reb-3527","parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"aa0b-92f6-c132-4c23","ticket_type":"task","title":"Guidance: require the MCP server for rebar ops (except local-code ops); document certified-op routing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["760b33c5-5ec3-47b9-82be-8d3a4a2423df","bfdf89c0-2a3b-4c21-b943-c8d694322b0a","69b5bc04-0755-4ad3-b7db-f5a3e71e055c","cc09c36a-9282-4278-b2df-7e1db8cb7ea3","ec6812ad-d761-48b2-96fa-4131581e7b03"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787603599762229001,"uuid":"71d06313-4e50-478d-85ca-224c4e01d64c"}